1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,950
Every monsoon the Gandak dances across Bihar. In 2026 it broke its record.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,950
The world's flood maps use C-band radar. Under trees and crops, it largely misses the water.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,950
NISAR's L-band SAR (synthetic aperture radar) sees through: 17 km² of flooding Sentinel-1 called dry.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,950
Tap any field and hear its radar change as the water arrives.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,950
On open water: F1 0.05 for NISAR and 0.17 for Sentinel-1, checked against optical satellites.
